      6.7 Summary
         Building a business is described as a process that can be learned and mastered by
         talented and educated entrepreneurs by developing the following descriptions:
         ■   Opportunity, vision, value proposition, and business model.
         ■   Concept, feasibility, and story.
         ■   Financial plan, legal form, and business plan.
         ■   Resource acquisition plan.
         ■   Execution and launch process.
         We note that entrepreneurs have a story and business plan that helps them to
         codify and communicate their roadmap to achievement. Most entrepreneurs
         benefit from putting this plan into written form to sharpen their thinking, commu-
         nicate it well to others, and enable testing of critical assumptions and hypothesis.


